-- title:
--   Existence of lifts along arbitrary square-zero thickenings
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $r$ and a characteristic-zero domain $\mathcal{O}$ which is a discrete valuation ring, together with an irreducible element $\pi$ such that $\mathcal{O}$ is $(\pi)$-adically complete, $\mathcal{O}/(\pi)$ has exactly $r$ elements, and $(r)=(\pi)$; let $K_0$ be a characteristic-zero field that is a fraction field of $\mathcal{O}$, and $O^{nr}$ a characteristic-zero domain over $\mathcal{O}$ which is complete for the ideal generated by the image of $\pi$, with that ideal maximal, every element of $O^{nr}$ satisfying a monic $\mathcal{O}$-polynomial modulo it, and every monic $O^{nr}$-polynomial of positive degree having a root modulo it. Let $G$ be a type and $f_N : N \to \operatorname{Spec}\mathcal{O}$ a morphism of schemes locally of finite type. Write $F$ for the functor on $\mathcal{O}$-algebras sending $B$ to $((O^{nr} \to_{\mathcal{O}} B) \times \mathrm{DeligneDatum}(K_0,\pi,B)) \times G$, where a Deligne datum is a family of $B$-submodules $\mathrm{line}(M) \subseteq B \otimes_{\mathcal{O}} M$ indexed by the full $\mathcal{O}$-lattices $M$ in $K_0^2$, with invertible quotients, monotone under inclusions of lattices, equivariant for scalar homotheties, and nondegenerate at every prime of $B$; the maps of $F$ are composition, base change of lines, and the identity on $G$. Write $\hat N(B)$ for the set of morphisms $\varphi : \operatorname{Spec} B \to N$ with $\varphi$ followed by $f_N$ the structural morphism $\operatorname{Spec} B \to \operatorname{Spec}\mathcal{O}$. Given maps $\Theta_B : F(B) \to \hat N(B)$ for all $\mathcal{O}$-algebras $B$ in which $\pi$ is nilpotent, natural in $\mathcal{O}$-algebra maps between such algebras, assume the unique lifting property: whenever $p : B \to B_0$ is a surjective $\mathcal{O}$-algebra map with $\pi$ nilpotent in $B$ and $B_0$, $B$ Noetherian, and the kernel of $p$ of square zero (any two elements killed by $p$ have product $0$), each $x_0 \in F(B_0)$ and $y \in \hat N(B)$ with $\hat N(p)(y) = \Theta_{B_0}(x_0)$ admit a unique $x \in F(B)$ with $F(p)(x) = x_0$ and $\Theta_B(x) = y$. The conclusion drops the Noetherian hypothesis and asserts existence only: for any such $p$, $x_0$, $y$ with $\hat N(p)(y) = \Theta_{B_0}(x_0)$, there exists $x \in F(B)$ with $F(p)(x) = x_0$ and $\Theta_B(x) = y$.
--
--   This is the existence half of the passage from formal étaleness of $\Theta$ tested on Noetherian square-zero thickenings to formal étaleness over arbitrary ones, in the setting of the Čerednik–Drinfeld comparison between the formal upper half-plane functor and a formal scheme over $\mathcal{O}$. It is used by [`CerednikDrinfeld.FormalOmega.forall_existsUnique_lift_of_forall_isNoetherianRing_existsUnique_lift`](thm.html#CerednikDrinfeld.FormalOmega.forall_existsUnique_lift_of_forall_isNoetherianRing_existsUnique_lift), which combines it with the corresponding uniqueness statement.
